  "homeActivities": [
    {
      "text": "Activity 1 — Float or sink\nFill a bowl or the sink. Line up: an apple, a stone, a closed plastic bottle, a metal spoon, a coin, a cork, a plastic pot, a small ball. He predicts\nevery single one first and you write the guesses in two columns. Then drop them in one at a time and check.\nA lovely question to leave hanging: \"A small metal nail sinks — so how does a huge metal ship float?\" You do not have to answer it.\nWondering is the point.\nActivity 2 — Make a sailboat\nFold a small boat from aluminium foil. Push a straw through a paper square to make a sail and stand it in the boat. Float it in the bowl and\nblow. Then ask: \"Did I push it or pull it?\" (A push — with air.)\nthese FLOAT on top\napple bottle cork\nstone coin spoon\nthese SINK to the bottom\nDraw this tank on paper and let him place each object himself before you test it.\n",
      "safety": "An adult stays with the child for every activity. No glass, no sockets, no flames, and nothing small enough to swallow is left with a child\nalone. Water activities are done in a bowl or the sink, never near electrical items.",
      "pages": [
        15,
        16
      ],
